        "common_asset": "linuxROS2AutowareRuntime",
        "confirmed_in_graph": true,
        "disposition": "recorded; the split execution-domain representation of the superset is owned by INC-MW-011 (owner decision D6, 2026-10-15), not by the scope alignment",
        "statement": "The governed scope classifies the Linux/ROS 2 Autoware runtime as common to both planned members. The shared-asset superset has a single osPlatform slot, which the AAOS-integrated alternative binds to android (the vehicle-platform domain) while the Autoware application domain keeps its Linux runtime. The superset cannot express the split topology, so the common runtime has no superset realization dependency and osPlatform is bound per alternative.",
        "variation": "osPlatform"
      }
